  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_3",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s3"
      },
      "text": "While the communication models shifted dramatically between Gen 1 and Gen 2, both generations of Hikit retain the same basic RAT function consisting of remote command shell, file management, network proxy and port forwarding.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "Both Gen 1 and Gen 2 sub-families of Hikit consist of a main DLL (referred to as “the DLL”) that contains the RAT functionality; a kernel driver (referred to as “the Driver”) with Gen 2 also employs an additional component: a loader executable.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s2"
      },
      "text": "For Gen 1.0 and Gen 1.1 samples, the file path of the Hikit source code is consistently h:\\JmVodServer\\hikit .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "Starting with Gen 1.2, the file path switches to e:\\SourceCode\\hikit_new .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "In Gen 1.0 and Gen 1.1, the DLL instructs the Driver to listen for a specific string (typically a HTTP request string) and responds with another string.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s5"
      },
      "text": "In Gen 1.2, the Driver has a hardcoded trigger string (a specific HTTP request string) and the DLL instructs the Driver to inspect a specific HTTP header field for a specific hexadecimal value.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_14",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s8"
      },
      "text": "This places Gen 1.2 into a more stealth position as a random, non-HTTP compliant response from Gen 1.0 and Gen 1.1 samples is more obvious than a legitimate HTTP response with a specially crafted Etag header.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s9"
      },
      "text": "Gen 2.1 represents the first Gen 2 sub-generation to use an executable-based loader, DLL and driver model, a model that all subsequent Gen 2 sub-generations employ.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s1"
      },
      "text": "Gen 2.2 is notable for altering where the configuration information of the RAT is stored and using both DLL-based and executable- based loaders.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_17",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "Gen 2.3 is notable for its use of a legitimate SSL certificate as part of the handshake between the infected machine and the attacker’s C2.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_18",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s3"
      },
      "text": "Also, while Gen 2.1 and Gen 2.2 retain the configuration within the DLL component, Gen 2.3 stores the configuration within the loader component.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_27",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s2"
      },
      "text": "In order to hide services, the Driver will access the memory of the services.exe process, locate the linked list of services and remove the service entry that the Driver wishes to hide.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s3"
      },
      "text": "Upon activation, the Driver will expose its interface by calling IoCreateDevice with the name \\Device\\agony (for Gen 2.0 Beta samples), \\Device\\HTTPS (for Gen 2.1 samples), \\Device\\advcachemgr (for Gen 2.2 samples) or \\Device\\diskdump (for Gen 2.3 samples).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_36",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 10,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p10_s1"
      },
      "text": "In order for the DLL to load, Gen 2 (starting with Gen 2.1) uses a loader application (referred to simply as “the Loader”).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_45",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 13,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p13_s4"
      },
      "text": "Export Name Description DllRegisterServer If the Gen 2 RAT is running, waits for the RAT to shut down before returning.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_46",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 13,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p13_s5"
      },
      "text": "MatrixMain Activates the Gen 2 RAT (called from a stand-alone Loader) SetModuleHandle The given parameter becomes the new module handle for the RAT.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_47",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 13,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p13_s6"
      },
      "text": "StartServer Activates the Gen 2 RAT (called from a DLL Loader) StopServer Stops the Gen 2 RAT (called from a DLL Loader)",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_51",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 14,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p14_s4"
      },
      "text": "This allows an attacker to establish several Gen2 infections within a victim’s infrastructure and if outbound connectivity is prohibited for any of the infected machines, the attacker can route commands to the pseudo-isolated infections through accessible infected machines providing a high level of persistence to the malware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_53",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 14,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p14_s6"
      },
      "text": "Each communication burst (either between the malware and the C2 or the malware and neighboring malware) begins with a 24-byte header identical to the header found in Gen 1.2.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_55",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 15,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p15_s1"
      },
      "text": "Support Software In addition to the main Hikit malware, there are at least two examples of support programs that belong to the Hikit family.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_56",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 15,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p15_s2"
      },
      "text": "The console is a text based application that takes a Gen 1.0 or Gen 1.2 infection’s IP address and proceeds to connect and authenticate with the infected server.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_57",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
        "page": 15,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p15_s3"
      },
      "text": "Once connected, the operator has the basic Hikit functionalities available to them via commands such as file and shell .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_59",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Hikit_Analysis-Final",
      "locator": {
